@page "/components/ai/messageactions"
@inherits AppComponentBase

<PageOutlet Url="components/ai/messageactions"
            Title="AiMessageActions"
            Description="BitAiMessageActions is the row under a finished AI reply: copy, regenerate and thumbs up or down, plus the model, the token usage and the time the options in force show." />

<DemoPage Name="AiMessageActions"
          Description="BitAiMessageActions is the row under a finished assistant message: copy, regenerate (with a session, for the newest reply) and thumbs up or down feedback, plus extra buttons of the app's own, and the metadata the BitAiUiOptions in force choose to show - the model, the token usage, the time. The actions are revealed while the message is hovered or holds the focus; the metadata is always shown. BitAiChatMessage renders one under every reply."
          Parameters="componentParameters"
          SubClasses="componentSubClasses"
          SubEnums="componentSubEnums"
          CssVariables="componentCssVariables"
          GitHubAIUrl="MessageActions/BitAiMessageActions.razor"
          GitHubDemoUrl="AI/MessageActions/BitAiMessageActionsDemo.razor">
    <NotesTemplate>
        <BitText>
            To use this component, you need to install the
            <BitLink Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Bit.BlazorUI.AI" Target="_blank">
                <BitTag Reversed
                        Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI"
                        Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground"
                        IconName="@BitIconName.NavigateExternalInline" />
            </BitLink>
            nuget package, as described in the Optional steps of the
            <BitLink Href="/getting-started">Getting started</BitLink> page.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            Copy and feedback work on the <b>Message</b> alone; regenerate needs the <b>Session</b> that drives it. What the row
            shows follows the <BitLink Href="/components/ai/optionsprovider">BitAiUiOptions</BitLink> in force:
            <b>ShowMessageActions</b> for the buttons, <b>ShowModelName</b>, <b>ShowUsage</b> and <b>ShowTimestamps</b> for the
            metadata (this site turns the model and the usage on). The model is shown by the name the registered model catalog
            (<b>ai.AddModels</b>) gives it, its id otherwise; the time in the <b>TimeZone</b> of the options, else in the
            reader's own zone, which the browser is asked for once the row has rendered. The <b>datetime</b> of the time
            element is the instant itself, in UTC.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            The buttons are named for a screen reader and a pressed feedback button says so through <b>aria-pressed</b>, its glyph
            drawn solid and in the primary color, so the choice is never carried by the color alone. The hidden actions are
            only faded out: they stay reachable with the keyboard, and they are always shown on a touch screen, on a phone-wide
            screen, under a preference for more contrast, and when <b>Pinned</b>. A printout keeps the metadata and leaves the
            buttons out.
        </BitText>
    </NotesTemplate>
    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" Id="example1">
            <div>
                Give it the <b>Message</b> it belongs to: hover the row, or tab to it, to reveal copy and feedback. The metadata
                beside them is never hidden: the model and the token usage here, which this site's options turn on
                (<b>ShowModelName</b> and <b>ShowUsage</b> are off by default; see the Options example).
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>@message.GetText()</div>
            <BitAiMessageActions Message="message" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Pinned" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2">
            <div>
                <b>Pinned</b> keeps the actions visible rather than revealing them on hover - for the newest reply, or a row
                rendered on its own.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>@pinnedMessage.GetText()</div>
            <BitAiMessageActions Pinned Message="pinnedMessage" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Feedback" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3">
            <div>
                <b>OnFeedback</b> reports the sentiment the user picked - and <b>None</b> when they press the chosen one again
                to withdraw it. The message's <b>Feedback</b> is already updated, so a host only has to persist it. Under a
                BitAiChatMessage, a BitAiMessageList or a BitAiChat, the same choice reaches their own <b>OnFeedback</b> as a
                <BitLink Href="/components/ai/chatmessage#message-feedback">BitAiMessageFeedback</BitLink>, paired with its
                message. <b>ShowFeedback</b> takes the thumbs away.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>@feedbackMessage.GetText()</div>
            <BitAiMessageActions Pinned Message="feedbackMessage" OnFeedback="HandleFeedback" />
            <br />
            <div>Last feedback: <b>@lastFeedback</b></div>
            <br />
            <div>@noFeedbackMessage.GetText()</div>
            <BitAiMessageActions Pinned ShowFeedback="false" Message="noFeedbackMessage" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Regenerate" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example4CsharpCode" Id="example4">
            <div>
                With a <b>Session</b>, the row offers regenerate, which discards the reply and asks again. Only the newest reply
                should offer it - regenerating an older one discards everything after it - so <b>CanRegenerate</b> turns it off
                for the others.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitToggle @bind-Value="canRegenerate" Text="CanRegenerate" />
            @if (regenerateSession.Conversation.LastMessage is { } reply)
            {
                @if (reply.IsBusy)
                {
                    <div>Regenerating...</div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div>@reply.GetText()</div>
                    <BitAiMessageActions Pinned
                                         Message="reply"
                                         Session="regenerateSession"
                                         CanRegenerate="canRegenerate" />
                }
            }
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Extra actions" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
            <div>
                <b>ExtraActionsTemplate</b> appends buttons of the app's own to the row - a bookmark, here. Draw them like the
                built-in ones: text buttons with a glyph, a title and an accessible name.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>@extraMessage.GetText()</div>
            <BitAiMessageActions Pinned Message="extraMessage">
                <ExtraActionsTemplate>
                    <BitButton Variant="BitVariant.Text"
                               IconName="@(isBookmarked ? BitIconName.SingleBookmarkSolid : BitIconName.SingleBookmark)"
                               Title="@(isBookmarked ? "Remove the bookmark" : "Bookmark")"
                               AriaLabel="@(isBookmarked ? "Remove the bookmark" : "Bookmark")"
                               aria-pressed="@(isBookmarked ? "true" : "false")"
                               OnClick="ToggleBookmark" />
                </ExtraActionsTemplate>
            </BitAiMessageActions>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Options" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6">
            <div>
                What the row shows is the <b>BitAiUiOptions</b> in force, cascaded by a
                <BitLink Href="/components/ai/optionsprovider">BitAiOptionsProvider</BitLink>: the first shows the time too, the
                second only the metadata (<b>ShowMessageActions</b> off).
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiOptionsProvider UiOptions="allMetadataOptions">
                <div>@optionsMessage.GetText()</div>
                <BitAiMessageActions Pinned Message="optionsMessage" />
            </BitAiOptionsProvider>
            <br />
            <BitAiOptionsProvider UiOptions="metadataOnlyOptions">
                <div>@metadataOnlyMessage.GetText()</div>
                <BitAiMessageActions Message="metadataOnlyMessage" />
            </BitAiOptionsProvider>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example7CsharpCode" Id="example7">
            <div>
                A disabled row keeps its metadata and disables its buttons (copy, regenerate, feedback).
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitToggle @bind-Value="isDisabled" Text="Disabled" />
            <div>@disabledMessage.GetText()</div>
            <BitAiMessageActions Pinned Disabled="isDisabled" Message="disabledMessage" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Cascading parameters" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example8CsharpCode" Id="example8">
            <div>
                <b>BitParams</b> with a <b>BitAiMessageActionsParams</b> sets what the rows of an app agree on - whether they
                are pinned, whether they offer feedback, their classes and styles - for every row inside it; a row's own value
                wins (the second keeps its feedback). <b>Pinned</b> and <b>ShowFeedback</b> reach the rows a BitAiChatMessage
                renders under its replies too, while their classes and styles come from the message's own
                <b>Styles</b> / <b>Classes</b> (its <b>MessageActions</b> member).
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitParams Parameters="actionsParams">
                <div>@cascadeMessage.GetText()</div>
                <BitAiMessageActions Message="cascadeMessage" />
                <br />
                <div>@cascadeOwnMessage.GetText()</div>
                <BitAiMessageActions ShowFeedback Message="cascadeOwnMessage" />
            </BitParams>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example9CsharpCode" Id="example9">
            <div>
                <b>Style</b> / <b>Class</b> reach the root, <b>Styles</b> / <b>Classes</b> each part (the group of buttons,
                the regenerate and feedback buttons with the class-styles of BitButton, the model and the time). The public
                <b>--bit-AiMessageActions-*</b> variables (see the CSS variables table) re-skin it from <b>:root</b>, an
                ancestor or <b>Style</b>.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>
                <BitAiMessageActions Pinned
                                     Message="styleMessage"
                                     Style="padding:0.25rem 0.5rem;border-radius:1rem;background:var(--bit-clr-bg-sec)"
                                     Styles="@(new() { Model = "font-weight:bold", FeedbackButton = new() { Icon = "color:tomato" } })" />
                <br />
                <BitAiMessageActions Pinned
                                     Message="classMessage"
                                     Class="custom-actions"
                                     Classes="@(new() { Actions = "custom-actions-group", Model = "custom-actions-model" })" />
                <br />
                <BitAiMessageActions Pinned
                                     Message="variablesMessage"
                                     Style="--bit-AiMessageActions-gap:2rem;--bit-AiMessageActions-actions-gap:0.5rem;--bit-AiMessageActions-color:var(--bit-clr-pri);--bit-AiMessageActions-font-size:0.875rem" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example10RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example10CsharpCode" Id="example10">
            <div>Use BitAiMessageActions in right-to-left (RTL).</div>
            <br />
            <div dir="rtl">@rtlMessage.GetText()</div>
            <BitAiMessageActions Pinned Dir="BitDir.Rtl" Message="rtlMessage" />
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>
</DemoPage>
